## Data & Access Control (Target; verify against actual schema)
| Table | Read | Write |
|---|---|---|
| profiles | Public | UPDATE owner only; row created via `handle_new_user` trigger |
| community_posts | Public | INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE owner only |
| messages | Conversation participants only | Participants only; sender = `auth.uid()` |
| notifications | Recipient only (`user_id`) | Created by triggers; recipient updates `is_read` only |
| products | Public | ViciTech admins only |
| partners | Public | ViciTech admins only (confirm) |

Storage: `post-media` (public read, authenticated upload only, size limits enforced). `audio-tracks` (public read, admin write; confirm).

## Architectural Constraints (Never Violate)
1. Default to Server Components. Place `'use client'` only on the smallest leaf components requiring interactivity, state, or browser APIs.
2. Perform first-party mutations via Server Actions. Use Route Handlers only for webhooks, external endpoints, and streaming.
3. Enforce authorization on the server (layouts, pages, actions) and via RLS. Use Middleware only for session refresh and optimistic redirects.
4. Modify database schemas strictly via SQL migrations. Every exposed table must have RLS enabled.
5. Keep secrets and `service_role` keys strictly on the server.
6. Design mobile-first for `360px` to `414px` viewports. Zero horizontal overflow allowed.
7. Treat `DESIGN.md` as the single source of truth for all visual and UI decisions.
8. Execute one module at a time according to the Definition of Done in `docs/ROADMAP.md`.
9. Write all user-facing UI text in natural Indonesian (keeping standard technical terms like GPU, RAM, FPS in English).
10. Use generated types from `types/database.types.ts` for all database queries and mutations. Regenerate after every migration.
11. Wrap mandatory atomic multi-table writes in a single Postgres function (RPC) rather than sequential queries in Server Actions.

## Roadmap Summary (Details in `docs/ROADMAP.md`)
1. **Phase 1:** Auth & cache hardening, global navigation, real-time notifications, welcome page.
2. **Phase 2:** Multi-category feed, media uploads, audio backsound, gaming LFG.
3. **Phase 3:** Catalog schema, `/market` storefront, product details, preset setups & creator verdicts.
4. **Phase 4:** YouTube embeds, partner directory & Google Maps, social share & dynamic OG tags.
5. **Phase 5:** RLS security audit, performance & mobile optimization, data seeding & demo readiness.

